<title>FRANCE: Two ships loading flour at Rouen, two more due.</title>
<headline>Two ships loading flour at Rouen, two more due.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two ships are loading a total of 9,600 tonnes of flour at Rouen, officials at the northern French port said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The flour will be exported to West Africa and Algeria, they said.</p>
<p>Two more vessels are expected in port between October 17 and 20 to load 23,700 tonnes of flour, they said.</p>
<p>Details on destination were not available.</p>
</text>
